`libgeozl` statically links the following software.

  OpenZL b7f498b         BSD 3-Clause     licenses/LICENSE.OpenZL
  xxHash, in OpenZL       BSD 2-Clause     licenses/LICENSE.xxHash
  pdqsort, in OpenZL      zlib             licenses/LICENSE.pdqsort
  Zstandard 1.5.7         BSD 3-Clause     licenses/LICENSE.Zstandard
  LZ4 1.10.0 (lib only)   BSD 2-Clause     licenses/LICENSE.LZ4

Only LZ4's BSD-licensed `lib` directory is built.

The npm package adds what Emscripten links. `geozl.wasm` contains musl and
`geozl.js` is Emscripten's runtime. `geozl.wasm` also contains LLVM compiler-rt
builtins, whose LLVM exception needs no notice in compiled form, and dlmalloc,
which is in the public domain.

  musl                    MIT              licenses/LICENSE.musl
  Emscripten              MIT or NCSA      licenses/LICENSE.Emscripten

The R source package also carries these zstd sources, which nothing links.

  divsufsort, in zstd     MIT              licenses/LICENSE.divsufsort
  JoinPaths, in zstd      MIT or CC0-1.0   licenses/LICENSE.JoinPaths

Where each distribution keeps the licence texts:

  Wheels                  <name>.dist-info/licenses/, the libgeozl list only
  libgeozl tarballs       licenses/, also in the Julia artifacts
  npm package             licenses/
  R source package        inst/licenses/
  CMake install           share/licenses/geozl/
